Fillets: at an OnSame end whose prolongation runs from the corner's vertex
along a seam of the opposite face that ends there, the prolongation is not
split where it meets the seam at its own start (mitcad#1359).

PerformOneCorner's OnSame end prolongs the edge between the face at the end
and the opposite face from the corner's vertex to the opposite contact's
end (the VARIANT1 curve), and splits that curve where it crosses a seam of
the opposite face (intcouture), at the extremum of the seam's edge and the
curve that BRepExtrema_ExtCC finds at distance 0. A boss's foot rounded on
a plate's top up to the plate's flat sides, which go on tangentially into
the boss's cylinder: at the vertex where the cylinder's seam starts, the
prolongation runs up the seam's line from the vertex, and the extremum lay
at the vertex, the curve's start (the seam and the curve at parameter 15,
the plate's height, not found parallel): the curve was split into a piece
from 15 to 15, and Geom_TrimmedCurve threw "U1 == U2" (the rounding failed
at that vertex for every radius). As for the cap's own crossing of the seam
below, a crossing at one of the curve's ends (within tolapp3d) is no
crossing; the curve stays whole, and the seam along it is cut at its end
as patch 0147 does (ChFi3d_CutSeamAlongCurve).

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_boss_tangent.cpp, the boss's foot rounded
with 1, 3 and 6 with the cylinder's seam at either vertex and on the body
MitCad's sketch and extrusions build (MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES): valid, the
material added as the exact ring between the sides within 1e-6 of it.

Upstream: new.

